# ──── API key authentication (pilot / production) ────
# When API_KEY is set, every /api/v1/* endpoint (except /health,
# /healthz and /health/ready) requires an `X-API-Key: <value>`
# header. Missing header → 401, wrong value → 403.
# When API_KEY is NOT set, security is disabled — convenient for
# local dev, NEVER deploy this way at a customer.
# Frontend reads NEXT_PUBLIC_API_KEY at build time and includes it
# automatically (see frontend/src/lib/api/client.ts).
# Generate a strong key: `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# API_KEY=replace-with-a-strong-random-string